# ===========================================================================
# What each published file is: its media type, from the model. The generated headers
# file is written from these, so no rule is written by hand. A media type is an IANA media
# type with the charset a text type is served with. servedUnaided says the platform's own
# answer for the file already is the type named here (measured, and checked on every run
# against a server); a file it does not hold gets a rule. cacheControl is what a file that
# must reach the reader as the exact bytes in the repository is served with.
# ===========================================================================
<https://drift-king.org/ah/site/charset> a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "charset" ;
    rdfs:comment "The charset a text media type is served with." .
<https://drift-king.org/ah/site/cacheControl> a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "cache control" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Cache-Control a published file is served with." .
<https://drift-king.org/ah/site/servedUnaided> a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "served unaided" ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the platform, with no rule for the file, already answers with exactly the media type the model names for it." .
